HEL 10) and installed it as a trusted system CA via update-ca-trust. Verified functionally by issuing a leaf certificate and confirming it validates against the system default trust store, both before and after a full node restart (boot ID changed, confirming a genuine reboot).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS (RHEL 10.0) and found openssl missing; installed it via dnf\",\"Generated CA private key and self-signed root certificate (CN=OS Comparison Root CA, O=OS Comparison, 4096-bit RSA, SHA256, 10yr validity) under /etc/pki/ca-os-comparison/\",\"Copied the CA certificate to /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/ and ran update-ca-trust extract to install it as a trusted system CA\",\"Verified the CA appears in `trust list` as an anchor and in the system ca-bundle.crt\",\"Issued a leaf certificate signed by the new CA and confirmed `openssl verify` (using only the system default trust store) returned OK, proving functional trust\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline, restarted node1 via `shutdown -r now`, polled until the node was reachable again, and confirmed the boot_id changed (proving a real reboot)\",\"Post-reboot, re-verified the CA anchor, ca-bundle entry, and anchor file persisted, and re-ran the leaf-certificate issue+verify test to prove the trust configuration survived and is functionally working after restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"CA created with correct name (OS Comparison Root CA) on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-081640370aaf4d8d\",\"cmd-ef1996d26d724997\"],\"summary\":\"Generated rootCA.key and rootCA.crt; openssl x509 -subject confirms CN=OS Comparison Root CA, O=OS Comparison, self-signed (issuer==subject)\"},{\"requirement\":\"CA certificate installed as trusted system CA\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ef1996d26d724997\",\"cmd-4742eb08631743ef\"],\"summary\":\"Copied cert to /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/ and ran update-ca-trust extract; `trust list` shows it as a trust:anchor entry and it appears once in /etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt\"},{\"requirement\":\"Functional proof the CA is trusted system-wide (not just present in a list)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-71e7969d9f104abb\"],\"summary\":\"Issued a leaf certificate signed by the new CA and ran `openssl verify` with no explicit CA file (system default trust store) — result: leaf.crt: OK\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline / boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3596516593844f8c\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id=19062a82-6390-435d-a09f-4dba1593d529 and confirmed CA anchor/trust status prior to restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cb0ec75a6bd5461c\"],\"summary\":\"Issued `shutdown -r now` in background; exec stream closed as node went down, confirming the restart command was accepted and executed\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart availability and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-00fd032a9d354a56\",\"cmd-afadd14c5c56449f\",\"cmd-59d3211205d04468\"],\"summary\":\"Polled node1 (two timeouts while down, then success); boot_id changed to b03e9a91-4e57-4060-b92b-1c2d67e0f9f9, proving an actual reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of CA trust configuration and functional health\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-008669a2f05c43b4\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, `trust list` still shows OS Comparison Root CA as anchor, ca-bundle.crt still contains it, anchor file intact, and a freshly issued leaf cert verified OK against the system trust store\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created a local root CA named \"OS Comparison Root CA\" on node1 (RHEL 10) and installed it as a trusted system CA via update-ca-trust. Verified functionally by issuing a leaf certificate and confirming it validates against the system default trust store, both before and after a full node restart (boot ID changed, confirming a genuine reboot).","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS (RHEL 10.0) and found openssl missing; installed it via dnf","Generated CA private key and self-signed root certificate (CN=OS Comparison Root CA, O=OS Comparison, 4096-bit RSA, SHA256, 10yr validity) under /etc/pki/ca-os-comparison/","Copied the CA certificate to /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/ and ran update-ca-trust extract to install it as a trusted system CA","Verified the CA appears in `trust list` as an anchor and in the system ca-bundle.crt","Issued a leaf certificate signed by the new CA and confirmed `openssl verify` (using only the system default trust store) returned OK, proving functional trust","Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline, restarted node1 via `shutdown -r now`, polled until the node was reachable again, and confirmed the boot_id changed (proving a real reboot)","Post-reboot, re-verified the CA anchor, ca-bundle entry, and anchor file persisted, and re-ran the leaf-certificate issue+verify test to prove the trust configuration survived and is functionally working after restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"CA created with correct name (OS Comparison Root CA) on node1","command_ids":["cmd-081640370aaf4d8d","cmd-ef1996d26d724997"],"summary":"Generated rootCA.key and rootCA.crt; openssl x509 -subject confirms CN=OS Comparison Root CA, O=OS Comparison, self-signed (issuer==subject)"},{"requirement":"CA certificate installed as trusted system CA","command_ids":["cmd-ef1996d26d724997","cmd-4742eb08631743ef"],"summary":"Copied cert to /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/ and ran update-ca-trust extract; `trust list` shows it as a trust:anchor entry and it appears once in /etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt"},{"requirement":"Functional proof the CA is trusted system-wide (not just present in a list)","command_ids":["cmd-71e7969d9f104abb"],"summary":"Issued a leaf certificate signed by the new CA and ran `openssl verify` with no explicit CA file (system default trust store) — result: leaf.crt: OK"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline / boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-3596516593844f8c"],"summary":"Captured boot_id=19062a82-6390-435d-a09f-4dba1593d529 and confirmed CA anchor/trust status prior to restart"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-cb0ec75a6bd5461c"],"summary":"Issued `shutdown -r now` in background; exec stream closed as node went down, confirming the restart command was accepted and executed"},{"requirement":"Node restart availability and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-00fd032a9d354a56","cmd-afadd14c5c56449f","cmd-59d3211205d04468"],"summary":"Polled node1 (two timeouts while down, then success); boot_id changed to b03e9a91-4e57-4060-b92b-1c2d67e0f9f9, proving an actual reboot occurred"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of CA trust configuration and functional health","command_ids":["cmd-008669a2f05c43b4"],"summary":"After reboot, `trust list` still shows OS Comparison Root CA as anchor, ca-bundle.crt still contains it, anchor file intact, and a freshly issued leaf cert verified OK against the system trust store"}]},"ttft_ms":1305,"type":"result","duration_ms":69413,"uuid":"88725152-962f-4d26-a2e5-26766926cbf7","ttft_stream_ms":767,"time_to_request_ms":48,"queued_turn_count":0}
